From 5b62c3f4c847a715e7e25dc8de3493d5a1d6dc28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:57:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The drawn bow's line is steered onto the reticle

Our own hero's drawn bow pointed off the reticle: the add-on's fixed
shoulder turn (0.7 rad) was chosen before the body faced the aim, and once it
did the turn swung the bow arm right; a steep aim also leaned the upper body
about the turned shoulders and rolled the bow.

Each frame the client now reads the bow's line, from the string hand through
the grip, against the line from the string hand to the reticle, and turns and
leans the shoulders a share of the way (`BodyTwist::turn_fix`, `lean_fix`),
so the bow and the arrow on it point at the reticle whatever the camera, the
facing or the clip. The lean turns about the aim's own right, not the turned
shoulders'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
